WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:06.470 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  it's the holiday season which for most  of us northern hemisphereians is  associated with winter fun  hot chocolate building snow people  arnold schwarzenegger and jingle all the  way put that cookie down  now and of course being late for work  because of this nonsense  so to keep up with the holiday spirit  what better location to visit in hyrule  than the tropical rainforest of farren  what there's no snow here in  fact i haven't seen a single snowflake  around christmas time for  years global warming man ah  another beautiful snowy day in good old  norway  alright that that doesn't count i mean  norway is basically part of the north  pole right  not really moving on to roundup this  year we'll be taking one final look at  the zonai ruins together with my friend  conrad from the commonwealth realm  in this video we will focus mostly on  the zonai ruins themselves the ones  located close to the spring of courage  meanwhile over on conrad's channel he  will be covering other locations in the  area and its ties to laurellen village  so put on your barbarian outfit grab  your machete and let's venture into the  domain  of the zonai  the farron province is one of my  favorite locations in breath of the wild  and could have been my favorite if not  held back by the absurd amount of rain  plaguing this area  but there's something about a dense  rainforest hiding all kinds of secrets  it reminds me of the tales of british  explorers like percy harrison who in the  early 19th century ventured into the  vast amazon jungles of south america in  search of a lost civilization  which you may or may not know from the  movie the lost city of zee  the city of zee huh that's a funny  coincidence  anyway tucked away inside the vast sea  of trees and vegetation of farren we  find countless of ancient structures  all with the same recognizable building  style of the zonai  repeating themes of serpents or dragons  owls  and boar though we do find identical  ruins in other parts of hyrule some of  which like typhlo ruins are actually  quite large and densely packed  it doesn't compete with the farron  province as a whole when it comes to the  sheer number of structures scattered  around  no kidding i actually ran out of stamps  trying to mark each and every one of  them on the map which is capped at 100  so it's safe to say that there are well  over a hundred buildings hidden around  these parts  despite the fact that almost the entire  province is littered with these ancient  relics from times unknown  only one section of the map is actually  named after this mysterious tribe that  being the zonai ruins located between  pegas woods and harker lake even the  spring of courage which has the largest  and most impressive zonai stoneworks  doesn't belong to the zonai ruins  though it is closely connected to it so  what was the actual purpose of the zonai  ruins and spring of courage in  particular  well to get a better picture of this we  first need to outline where the most  prominent structures are found in fahren  the zonai made a clear effort to mark  the start and end of their territory  indicated by either two pillars or  statues standing side by side the first  of which can be found in the farron  woods to the west of the province  this practically marks the border  letting any wanted or  unwanted visitor to know that they are  now entering the domain of the zona  a similar set of pillars are found on  the other side of the area when exiting  a bar of forest towards lorelei village  after which any trace of the zona stone  works and in between these two border  markers  is where all the zonai action seems to  have taken place  at the northern and southern borders of  the domain are mostly sectioned off by  natural cliff and mountains  looking at the map we see a clear  distinction between three different  areas  almost like districts which all seem to  have served different purposes  the first fork in the road is found  immediately at the border in the fire in  the woods which is the road leading  south into fueral plain however the  zonai didn't build any structures in  this area a plausible reason for this is  that as we can see on the map  the floral plane lies eerily close to  the main of the horse god melania  perhaps the zona wanted to show respect  for divine entities or maybe even  feared it and thus refrained from  crossing into his territory the second  branching path is found at the zona  ruins themselves after exiting pagos  woods  similar to the borders in farron woods  in a bar of forest two large pillars are  placed here as  indications that this is where you enter  the district leading towards the spring  of courage  and finally the last fork in the road is  found right after crossing the saryan  bridge  one road leads south towards martha's  landing after which any trace of the  zonai ends completely this road also  borders guccini plain  multiple so-called zonai towers are  found the other road leads further east  towards lake florida and is marked by  two giant owl statues which again seems  to serve as sort of a border marker to  show that this is where our new district  starts beyond this point we find a lot  of zonai made structures along both  sides of the florian river and even up  on plateaus surrounding florida falls  so there we have it three clearly  distinct districts  all marked by two large pillars or  statues standing on opposite sides of  the road and here is where we find  something rather interesting  each of these districts has their own  dominant building style  for instance the zona ruins area  predominantly houses dragon statues  while the lake floria area barely  features any dragons and instead we find  most of the owl statues here  which in turn are not found anywhere  near the zona ruins  and the guccini plain district features  neither and instead mostly consists of  towers and some stray walls the dragon  district  owl district and tower district if you  will so now let's return our focus to  the zonai ruins and spring of courage  aka the dragon district as the other two  will be thoroughly explored in conrad's  video  one of the most distinctive features  about this area compared to the others  aside from the plethora of dragon  statues is that we find next to no ruins  which look like they may have been used  to house people  we do find these large walls but it's  pretty clear that these were not part of  a larger structure  instead i'm guessing these are retaining  walls retaining walls is a building  technique which was perfected by the  romans and its function is to hold back  the soil and prevent erosion from  swallowing up your territory so they  simply prevent the upper level from  collapsing into the valley below  we find these walls at the spring of  courage too and it doesn't seem like  these walls were connected to some sort  of rooftop of any kind  meaning the whole place was open to the  elements and provided no shelter from  the rain  this in the absence of proper housing  leads me to believe that nobody actually  lived in these parts of the territory  instead it was likely a place purely  devoted to pilgrimage and worship  in a way it's very similar to the great  plateau which was a holy place for the  highlands and where they too  underwent spiritual quests or  pilgrimages to pay respect to their  deity and their ancient ancestors the  big difference being that whereas the  highlands worshiped goddess hylia the  zonai worshiped the dragon spirit farosh  and here is where we need to dive a bit  deeper into the religious aspects of the  zoning the hylians as mentioned before  are all about hylium which as you may  know is a divine being whose essence is  passed on within the royal bloodline  however hylia isn't the highest being in  this universe  she along with the world itself was  created by the three golden goddesses of  power  wisdom and courage then nehru and for  all  the zone eyes seem to have been more  old-school compared to the hylians  instead of worshiping hailia who is  basically but a mere demigod  compared to the goddesses of creation  their devotion was to this original  trinity which is reflected by the three  different statues they constructed all  over their domain  that being the dragon owl and boar  additionally because the zone themselves  were all about bravery  combat skills and magic their attention  was primarily focused on the dragon  serpent farish  who in turn is derived from the goddess  of courage for roar  they did acknowledge the other two  goddesses as well but because the virtue  of courage lay closest to the way of  life  this is by far the most dominant symbol  in their religion  it is highly likely that every zona had  to undergo this pilgrimage at some point  in their life perhaps it was even a test  of strength and courage a way to prove  your worth and officially receive the  title of a zonai warrior the road  leading up to the spring could have been  filled with monsters and traps  hurdles which needed to be overcome and  tested the bravery of every pilgrim  striving to become a strong warrior  finally when they managed to reach the  spring of courage they would pay their  respects to faroush and the ritual was  complete  after this they would receive the  barbarian armor ready to serve the zone  military this is of course speculation  and it could also be that the pilgrimage  towards the spring of courage was more  of a peaceful and spiritual kind  rather than a brutal test of courage  whatever the case may be  it's clear that the zonai valued courage  above anything else  the fact that they are described as  barbarians warlike and savage  doesn't automatically mean that they  were evil on the contrary they seem to  have been very well aware of the  existence of farosh and it's made clear  that the dragon spirits only show  themselves to those who they deem to be  worthy  most people in hyrule are completely  oblivious to them and can just  walk right past them without them  noticing interestingly enough  rumor mill volume 5 titled dragons  actually exist  states that there are multiple  eyewitness accounts across hyrule of  people claiming to have seen the dragons  floating around  here's the kicker though all these  witness accounts come from children  and the article continues to say that  children are pure of heart meaning they  would never lie the fact that only  lincoln youngsters are able to see  farosh  hints that it has something to do with  the purity of one's heart  by that definition the zonai may have  been pure of heart as well  and not the savages they were made out  to be at best they were misunderstood  because of their more primitive  lifestyle but it's clear that the zonai  possessed many talents which rivaled  that of the ancient hylians they were  clearly master stonemasons on par with  that of the hylian stone workers  they had a deep connection with nature  and their deity and the fact that the  ruins of their civilization have  survived the elements all this time  is a true testament to the dominance  they once exerted before  their sudden disappearance and that  wraps up today's video  be sure to head over to commonwealth  realm and check out conrad's video which  goes more in depth into the living  conditions of the zonai their traditions  skills and other interesting stuff found  in the other so-called districts within  farren  and of course a big thanks to conrad for  joining me in this video  as always a massive thanks to my  gracious patreons and channel members  a shout out goes to flavi my latest  patreon to join the cause  thank you so much for your support it  really  really means a lot anyway that is all  for now this is dawn  signing off and have a good one  [Music]  you

